    {
      "id": "seR_uEltvlrRXIcNAcZuZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3486.369047619041,
      "y": -1221.3333333333303,
      "width": 1080.2499999999993,
      "height": 1232.4999999999998,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 426741913,
      "version": 1277,
      "versionNonce": 578709016,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784233871580,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "NOTE: Do we want to aggregate\nthese groups of data and post them\nall at once on a schedule? For\nexample, even if we have 10 nodes,\neach with a single machine, should\nthey create snapshots, throw them\non a queue, and then every X interval\n(configurable?) the server would pop Y\n(configurable?) snapshots off the\nqueue and send them to the API?\nThere should also probably be a cap\non the number of queued batches to\nmake sure we're not consuming too\nmuch memory.\n\nThis could add a lot of performance\ntweaking for end users.",
      "fontSize": 57.999999999999986,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "NOTE: Do we want to aggregate these groups of data and post them all at once on a schedule? For example, even if we have 10 nodes, each with a single machine, should they create snapshots, throw them on a queue, and then every X interval (configurable?) the server would pop Y (configurable?) snapshots off the queue and send them to the API? There should also probably be a cap on the number of queued batches to make sure we're not consuming too much memory.\n\nThis could add a lot of performance  tweaking for end users.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "S8kEmsT24FYGDecx_nsKD",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -4800.964285714294,
      "y": -1004.3333333333303,
      "width": 1272.0000000000011,
      "height": 960.000000000001,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3W",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1428063639,
      "version": 1552,
      "versionNonce": 46959208,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784235062488,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Each Telemetry node is connected to a number of\nGregTech machines.\n\nEach Node will have a configurable polling rate within\nits in-game 'on use' UI. Minimums are configurable via\nthe server.config / property files to prevent\nextremely small sample rates.\n\nOnce the polling interval is hit, Minecraft takes a\n\"snapshot\" of the Telemetry Node's 'network'. \n\nThis snapshot contains information such as the\nTelemetry Node, Name / Type of GregTech machine,\ncurrent recipe being created, etc. \n\nIt is bundled and added to a queue.",
      "fontSize": 48.00000000000005,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Each Telemetry node is connected to a number of GregTech machines.\n\nEach Node will have a configurable polling rate within its in-game 'on use' UI. Minimums are configurable via the server.config / property files to prevent extremely small sample rates.\n\nOnce the polling interval is hit, Minecraft takes a \"snapshot\" of the Telemetry Node's 'network'. \n\nThis snapshot contains information such as the Telemetry Node, Name / Type of GregTech machine, current recipe being created, etc. \n\nIt is bundled and added to a queue.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
